// CrossEngin NL Surface: grammar parser (ADR-0104 R48p2, expanded R97).
//
// LLM-free deterministic recognizer for the canonical question shapes
// documented in ADR-0104. Handles most well-formed questions on the
// domains we ship. Fast, auditable, no network.
//
// PROTOCOL:
//   grammar_parse(text) -> StructuredQuery
//     - empty / whitespace-only                    -> sq_none
//     - starts with '/'                            -> sq_unparsed (slash-cmd)
//     - filler-only (hi/hey/hello/um/uh/hmm)       -> sq_none
//     - matches a known pattern (after preamble
//       strip)                                     -> the corresponding sq_*
//     - anything else                              -> sq_unparsed (LLM fallback)
//
// R97 EXPANSION (Phase C part 2, metric-driven per ADR-0211).
//
// The 12 canonical shapes (R48p2) are extended to ~85+ natural phrasings
// that all resolve to the SAME 11 sq_* kinds -- no new SQ kinds are
// introduced. The R96 `nl.metrics` verb makes the effect on
// `fallback_rate` directly observable.
//
// Preamble stripping. Common polite/filler leading + trailing tokens
// (`please`, `can you`, `could you`, `would you`, `will you`,
// `may i ask`, `i want to`, `i would like to`, `i d like to`, `hey`,
// `hi there`, `hello there`) are removed BEFORE pattern matching so
// `please tell me about X` parses the same as `tell me about X`.
// Trailing `please`, `thanks`, `thank you` are stripped too. `not` is
// NEVER stripped (would change meaning).
//
// Recognized patterns (v2, in match-priority order; more-specific FIRST):
//
//   RESEARCH:
//     - `what do you know about X`             (5-word prefix)
//     - `what is the meaning of X`             (5-word prefix)
//     - `what can you say about X`             (5-word prefix)
//     - `what is the relationship between X and Y`  -> RELATE
//     - `what does X mean`                     ("mean" suffix)
//     - `tell me about X`                      (3-word prefix)
//     - `give me info on X` / `give me info about X` (4-word prefix)
//     - `key points about X`                   (3-word prefix)
//     - `find contradictions in X`             (3-word prefix)  -> CONTRADICT_SCAN
//     - `scan for contradictions about X`      (4-word prefix)  -> CONTRADICT_SCAN
//     - `explain X` / `describe X` / `define X` / `elaborate on X` / `expand on X`
//     - `information on X` / `information about X`
//     - `history of X` / `origin of X` / `overview of X` / `summary of X`
//     - `background on X` / `facts about X` / `details on X`
//     - `how does X work`                      (RESEARCH X)
//     - `why is X important`                   (RESEARCH X)
//     - `what is X / what are X / what was X / what were X`
//     - `X definition` / `X meaning` / `X explained`   (SUFFIX form)
//     - `know about X`                         (kicks in after `i want to` strip)
//     - `who {is/are/was/were} X`              -> RESEARCH (kind_filter="person")
//     - `when {did/was/is/were/are} X`         -> RESEARCH (kind_filter="event")
//     - `where {is/are/was/were} X`            -> RESEARCH (kind_filter="place")
//     - `why X` (loose fallback)
//
//   RELATE:
//     - `how does X relate to Y`
//     - `does X relate to Y`                   (existing)
//     - `how are X and Y related`
//     - `connection between X and Y`
//     - `link between X and Y`
//     - `association between X and Y`
//     - `similarities between X and Y`
//     - `difference between X and Y`           (differences ARE relations)
//     - `compare X and Y` / `comparison of X and Y`
//     - `X vs Y` / `X versus Y`
//
//   CONTRADICT_SCAN:
//     - `does X contradict Y`                  (existing; 2-topic)
//     - `contradictions in X`                  (1-topic; both slots = X)
//     - `conflicts about X`                    (1-topic)
//     - `disagreements about X`                (1-topic)
//     - `inconsistencies in X`                 (1-topic)
//     - `where does X conflict`                (1-topic)
//
//   IS_A:
//     - `is X a Y` / `is X an Y`               (existing; also strips leading
//                                                `kind of` / `type of` from Y)
//     - `is X a kind of Y` / `is X a type of Y`
//     - `is X kind of Y` / `is X type of Y`
//     - `is X considered Y` / `is X considered a Y`
//     - `does X count as Y` / `does X count as a Y`
//     - `X is a Y` / `X is an Y`               (declarative form)
//
//   RETRACT:
//     - `retract X`                            (existing)
//     - `retract fact X`
//     - `forget X` / `forget about X`
//     - `remove X` / `delete X` / `unlearn X` / `withdraw X`
//
//   CAPSULE_INSTALL:
//     - `install capsule X`                    (existing)
//     - `add capsule X` / `load capsule X` / `import capsule X`
//     - `enable capsule X` / `install pack X` (`pack` = capsule alias)
//
//   SKILL_INSTALL:
//     - `install skill X`                      (existing)
//     - `add skill X` / `load skill X` / `enable skill X` / `activate skill X`
//
//   CAPSULE_LIST:
//     - `list capsules` / `list capsule`       (existing)
//     - `list all capsules` / `show capsules` / `show all capsules`
//     - `what capsules are installed` / `which capsules do i have`
//     - `installed capsules` / `available capsules`
//
//   SKILL_LIST:
//     - `list skills` / `list skill`           (existing)
//     - `list all skills` / `show skills` / `show all skills`
//     - `what skills are available` / `which skills do i have`
//     - `installed skills` / `available skills`
//
//   SKILL_RUN:
//     - `run skill X on Y` / `run X on Y`      (existing)
//     - `execute X on Y` / `use skill X on Y` / `use X on Y`
//     - `invoke X on Y` / `apply X to Y` / `run X with Y`
//
//   NONE (empty semantics):
//     - Pure whitespace / punctuation-only (existing)
//     - Filler-only utterances (`um`, `uh`, `hmm`, `hi`, `hey`, `hello`,
//       `hi there`, `hello there`)  -- greetings aren't queries
//
// Multi-word slot values (X, Y) are joined with a single space so the
// downstream tokenizer (research_skill, persona_project) can split
// them again per its own rules. No underscoring here -- keeps the
// original user phrasing visible in traces.
//
// NOVA dependencies: builtins.
// CrossEngin dependencies: src/nl/query_shape.nova, src/util/str_safe.nova.

import "./query_shape.nova"
import "../util/str_safe.nova"

// ---- normalize + tokenize -------------------------------------------------

fn _gp_is_ws(c) {
    if c == 32 { return 1 }
    if c == 9  { return 1 }
    if c == 13 { return 1 }
    if c == 10 { return 1 }
    return 0
}

// Is `c` a "word" character we keep? ASCII letters + digits + '_' + '-'.
// Everything else (punctuation, apostrophes contracted) is skipped so
// the tokenizer produces clean per-word units.
fn _gp_is_wordchar(c) {
    if c >= 65 { if c <= 90  { return 1 } }
    if c >= 97 { if c <= 122 { return 1 } }
    if c >= 48 { if c <= 57  { return 1 } }
    if c == 95 { return 1 }         // '_'
    if c == 45 { return 1 }         // '-'
    return 0
}

fn _gp_lower_char(c) {
    if c >= 65 { if c <= 90 { return c + 32 } }
    return c
}

// Trim leading '/' + surrounding whitespace + trailing '?' or '.' from
// the raw text. The '/' check lets the caller re-run the slash-command
// dispatcher on inputs that start with one.
fn _gp_slash_prefixed(text) {
    let n = len(text)
    let i = 0
    while i < n {
        if _gp_is_ws(char_at(text, i)) == 1 { i = i + 1 }
        else { if char_at(text, i) == 47 { return 1 }
               else { return 0 } }
    }
    return 0
}

fn _gp_is_blank(text) {
    let n = len(text)
    let i = 0
    while i < n {
        if _gp_is_ws(char_at(text, i)) == 0 { return 0 }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return 1
}

// Split `text` into lowercase whitespace-separated word tokens.
// Punctuation is stripped (each word runs while chars are wordchars).
// Apostrophes / question marks / commas etc. act as token boundaries.
fn _gp_tokenize(text) {
    let out = list_new()
    let n = len(text)
    let start = 0 - 1
    let i = 0
    while i < n {
        let c = char_at(text, i)
        if _gp_is_wordchar(c) == 1 {
            if start < 0 { start = i }
        } else {
            if start >= 0 {
                push(out, _gp_lower_slice(text, start, i))
                start = 0 - 1
            }
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    if start >= 0 { push(out, _gp_lower_slice(text, start, n)) }
    return out
}

fn _gp_lower_slice(text, from, to) {
    let out = ""
    let i = from
    while i < to {
        out = out + chr(_gp_lower_char(char_at(text, i)))
        i = i + 1
    }
    return out
}

// ---- match helpers --------------------------------------------------------

// True if `tokens[start..start+n-1]` equals `words[0..n-1]`.
// (n = len(words). Out-of-range = mismatch.)
fn _gp_match_seq(tokens, start, words) {
    let n = len(words)
    if start + n > len(tokens) { return 0 }
    let i = 0
    while i < n {
        if str_eq_bytes(tokens[start + i], words[i]) == 0 { return 0 }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return 1
}

// Find the first index of `word` in tokens at or after `from`; -1 if absent.
fn _gp_find_token(tokens, word, from) {
    let i = from
    while i < len(tokens) {
        if str_eq_bytes(tokens[i], word) == 1 { return i }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return 0 - 1
}

// Find the first index i in [from, end) where tokens[i]==w1 and
// tokens[i+1]==w2. -1 if absent.
fn _gp_find_pair(tokens, w1, w2, from) {
    let i = from
    let last = len(tokens) - 1
    while i < last {
        if str_eq_bytes(tokens[i], w1) == 1 {
            if str_eq_bytes(tokens[i + 1], w2) == 1 { return i }
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return 0 - 1
}

// Join tokens[from..to) with a single space. Returns "" if the range
// is empty or invalid.
fn _gp_join(tokens, from, to) {
    if from >= to { return "" }
    if from < 0 { return "" }
    if to > len(tokens) { return "" }
    let out = tokens[from]
    let i = from + 1
    while i < to {
        out = out + " " + tokens[i]
        i = i + 1
    }
    return out
}

// Copy tokens[from..to) into a fresh list. Used by preamble stripping
// so pattern matchers can keep using tokens[0], tokens[1], ...
fn _gp_slice_new(tokens, from, to) {
    let out = list_new()
    if from < 0 { from = 0 }
    if to > len(tokens) { to = len(tokens) }
    let i = from
    while i < to {
        push(out, tokens[i])
        i = i + 1
    }
    return out
}

// ---- word-list convenience: build a list<string> from up to N words -----
//
// NOVA doesn't have literal list syntax that plays nicely with function
// arguments, so give _gp_match_seq's callers small builders.

fn _gp_w1(w1) {
    let l = list_new() push(l, w1) return l
}

fn _gp_w2(w1, w2) {
    let l = list_new() push(l, w1) push(l, w2) return l
}

fn _gp_w3(w1, w2, w3) {
    let l = list_new() push(l, w1) push(l, w2) push(l, w3) return l
}

fn _gp_w4(w1, w2, w3, w4) {
    let l = list_new()
    push(l, w1) push(l, w2) push(l, w3) push(l, w4)
    return l
}

fn _gp_w5(w1, w2, w3, w4, w5) {
    let l = list_new()
    push(l, w1) push(l, w2) push(l, w3) push(l, w4) push(l, w5)
    return l
}

fn _gp_w6(w1, w2, w3, w4, w5, w6) {
    let l = list_new()
    push(l, w1) push(l, w2) push(l, w3) push(l, w4) push(l, w5) push(l, w6)
    return l
}

// ---- filler / preamble helpers -------------------------------------------

// True if `tok` is a stand-alone filler / greeting token (all-lowercase).
fn _gp_is_filler_token(tok) {
    if str_eq_bytes(tok, "um")     == 1 { return 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tok, "uh")     == 1 { return 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tok, "hmm")    == 1 { return 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tok, "hi")     == 1 { return 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tok, "hey")    == 1 { return 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tok, "hello")  == 1 { return 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tok, "there")  == 1 { return 1 }  // "hi there"/"hello there"
    if str_eq_bytes(tok, "hola")   == 1 { return 1 }
    return 0
}

// True if EVERY token is a filler. Empty list is treated as filler-free
// (caller already handled blank input).
fn _gp_all_fillers(tokens) {
    let n = len(tokens)
    if n == 0 { return 0 }
    let i = 0
    while i < n {
        if _gp_is_filler_token(tokens[i]) == 0 { return 0 }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return 1
}

// Strip common polite/filler preambles from the front and back of the
// token list. Runs in a fixed-point loop so `please could you please X`
// collapses cleanly. Longest patterns tried first at each step.
// Never strips `not` or anything that would change meaning.
fn _gp_strip_preamble(tokens) {
    let start = 0
    let end = len(tokens)
    // --- leading ---
    let changed = 1
    while changed == 1 {
        changed = 0
        // 4-token leading phrases
        if start + 4 <= end {
            let t0 = tokens[start]
            let t1 = tokens[start + 1]
            let t2 = tokens[start + 2]
            let t3 = tokens[start + 3]
            // "i would like to"
            if str_eq_bytes(t0, "i") == 1 {
                if str_eq_bytes(t1, "would") == 1 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(t2, "like") == 1 {
                        if str_eq_bytes(t3, "to") == 1 {
                            start = start + 4  changed = 1
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            // "i d like to"  (from "i'd like to")
            if changed == 0 {
                if str_eq_bytes(t0, "i") == 1 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "d") == 1 {
                        if str_eq_bytes(t2, "like") == 1 {
                            if str_eq_bytes(t3, "to") == 1 {
                                start = start + 4  changed = 1
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        // 3-token leading phrases
        if changed == 0 {
            if start + 3 <= end {
                let u0 = tokens[start]
                let u1 = tokens[start + 1]
                let u2 = tokens[start + 2]
                // "may i ask"
                if str_eq_bytes(u0, "may") == 1 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(u1, "i") == 1 {
                        if str_eq_bytes(u2, "ask") == 1 {
                            start = start + 3  changed = 1
                        }
                    }
                }
                // "i want to"
                if changed == 0 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(u0, "i") == 1 {
                        if str_eq_bytes(u1, "want") == 1 {
                            if str_eq_bytes(u2, "to") == 1 {
                                start = start + 3  changed = 1
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        // 2-token leading phrases
        if changed == 0 {
            if start + 2 <= end {
                let v0 = tokens[start]
                let v1 = tokens[start + 1]
                let modal = 0
                if str_eq_bytes(v0, "can")   == 1 { modal = 1 }
                if str_eq_bytes(v0, "could") == 1 { modal = 1 }
                if str_eq_bytes(v0, "would") == 1 { modal = 1 }
                if str_eq_bytes(v0, "will")  == 1 { modal = 1 }
                if modal == 1 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(v1, "you") == 1 {
                        start = start + 2  changed = 1
                    }
                }
                // "hi there" / "hello there" / "hey there"
                if changed == 0 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(v1, "there") == 1 {
                        if str_eq_bytes(v0, "hi")    == 1 { start = start + 2  changed = 1 }
                        if changed == 0 {
                            if str_eq_bytes(v0, "hello") == 1 { start = start + 2  changed = 1 }
                        }
                        if changed == 0 {
                            if str_eq_bytes(v0, "hey")   == 1 { start = start + 2  changed = 1 }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        // 1-token leading fillers
        if changed == 0 {
            if start < end {
                let w0 = tokens[start]
                if str_eq_bytes(w0, "please") == 1 { start = start + 1  changed = 1 }
                if changed == 0 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(w0, "hey")    == 1 { start = start + 1  changed = 1 }
                }
                if changed == 0 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(w0, "hi")     == 1 { start = start + 1  changed = 1 }
                }
                if changed == 0 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(w0, "hello")  == 1 { start = start + 1  changed = 1 }
                }
                if changed == 0 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(w0, "um")     == 1 { start = start + 1  changed = 1 }
                }
                if changed == 0 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(w0, "uh")     == 1 { start = start + 1  changed = 1 }
                }
                if changed == 0 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(w0, "hmm")    == 1 { start = start + 1  changed = 1 }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    // --- trailing ---
    changed = 1
    while changed == 1 {
        changed = 0
        // 2-token trailing: "thank you"
        if end - 2 >= start {
            let l0 = tokens[end - 2]
            let l1 = tokens[end - 1]
            if str_eq_bytes(l0, "thank") == 1 {
                if str_eq_bytes(l1, "you") == 1 {
                    end = end - 2  changed = 1
                }
            }
        }
        // 1-token trailing
        if changed == 0 {
            if end - 1 >= start {
                let lt = tokens[end - 1]
                if str_eq_bytes(lt, "please") == 1 { end = end - 1  changed = 1 }
                if changed == 0 {
                    if str_eq_bytes(lt, "thanks") == 1 { end = end - 1  changed = 1 }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    if start == 0 { if end == len(tokens) { return tokens } }
    return _gp_slice_new(tokens, start, end)
}

// ---- research prefix matchers (multi-word specific ones FIRST) -----------

// "what do you know about X" (5 fixed tokens then topic)
fn _try_what_do_you_know_about(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 6 { return 0 }
    let prefix = _gp_w5("what", "do", "you", "know", "about")
    if _gp_match_seq(tokens, 0, prefix) == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 5, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "what is the meaning of X"
fn _try_what_is_the_meaning_of(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 6 { return 0 }
    let prefix = _gp_w5("what", "is", "the", "meaning", "of")
    if _gp_match_seq(tokens, 0, prefix) == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 5, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "what can you say about X"
fn _try_what_can_you_say_about(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 6 { return 0 }
    let prefix = _gp_w5("what", "can", "you", "say", "about")
    if _gp_match_seq(tokens, 0, prefix) == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 5, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "what is the relationship between X and Y" -> RELATE
fn _try_what_is_the_relationship_between(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 8 { return 0 }
    let prefix = _gp_w6("what", "is", "the", "relationship", "between", "$$$")
    // custom-check first 5 tokens then the 6th is topic, so build via find:
    let want = _gp_w5("what", "is", "the", "relationship", "between")
    if _gp_match_seq(tokens, 0, want) == 0 { return 0 }
    let and_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "and", 6)
    if and_idx < 0 { return 0 }
    let a = _gp_join(tokens, 5, and_idx)
    let b = _gp_join(tokens, and_idx + 1, len(tokens))
    if len(a) == 0 { return 0 }
    if len(b) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_relate(a, b, raw, "grammar")
}

// "what does X mean" -> RESEARCH X
fn _try_what_does_x_mean(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "what") == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "does") == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[len(tokens) - 1], "mean") == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens) - 1)
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "tell me about X" (existing pattern)
fn _try_tell_me_about(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    let prefix = _gp_w3("tell", "me", "about")
    if _gp_match_seq(tokens, 0, prefix) == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 3, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "give me info on/about X" (4-word prefix)
fn _try_give_me_info(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 5 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "give") == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "me")   == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[2], "info") == 0 { return 0 }
    let t3 = tokens[3]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t3, "on")    == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t3, "about") == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 4, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "key points about X"
fn _try_key_points_about(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    let prefix = _gp_w3("key", "points", "about")
    if _gp_match_seq(tokens, 0, prefix) == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 3, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "find contradictions in X" -> CONTRADICT_SCAN (single-topic; slot b=a)
fn _try_find_contradictions_in(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    let prefix = _gp_w3("find", "contradictions", "in")
    if _gp_match_seq(tokens, 0, prefix) == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 3, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_contradict_scan(topic, topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "scan for contradictions about X" -> CONTRADICT_SCAN
fn _try_scan_for_contradictions_about(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 5 { return 0 }
    let prefix = _gp_w4("scan", "for", "contradictions", "about")
    if _gp_match_seq(tokens, 0, prefix) == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 4, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_contradict_scan(topic, topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// Single-word prefix RESEARCH verbs: explain / describe / define
fn _try_explain_describe_define(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 2 { return 0 }
    let t0 = tokens[0]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "explain")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "describe") == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "define")   == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 1, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "elaborate on X" / "expand on X"
fn _try_elaborate_expand_on(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    let t0 = tokens[0]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "elaborate") == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "expand")    == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "on") == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "information on/about X"
fn _try_information_prefix(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "information") == 0 { return 0 }
    let t1 = tokens[1]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "on")    == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "about") == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// Two-word RESEARCH prefixes with the shape: <NOUN> <PREP> <TOPIC>
// - history of X   / origin of X   / overview of X   / summary of X
// - background on X / facts about X / details on X / details about X
fn _try_research_prefix2(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    let t0 = tokens[0]
    let t1 = tokens[1]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "history")    == 1 { if str_eq_bytes(t1, "of")    == 1 { ok = 1 } }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "origin")     == 1 { if str_eq_bytes(t1, "of")    == 1 { ok = 1 } }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "overview")   == 1 { if str_eq_bytes(t1, "of")    == 1 { ok = 1 } }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "summary")    == 1 { if str_eq_bytes(t1, "of")    == 1 { ok = 1 } }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "background") == 1 { if str_eq_bytes(t1, "on")    == 1 { ok = 1 } }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "facts")      == 1 { if str_eq_bytes(t1, "about") == 1 { ok = 1 } }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "details")    == 1 { if str_eq_bytes(t1, "on")    == 1 { ok = 1 } }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "details")    == 1 { if str_eq_bytes(t1, "about") == 1 { ok = 1 } }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "know about X" -- catches "i want to know about X" after preamble strip
fn _try_know_about(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "know")  == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "about") == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "how does X work" -> RESEARCH X
fn _try_how_does_x_work(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "how")  == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "does") == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[len(tokens) - 1], "work") == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens) - 1)
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "why is X important" -> RESEARCH X
fn _try_why_is_x_important(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "why") == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "is")  == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[len(tokens) - 1], "important") == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens) - 1)
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// SUFFIX form: `X definition` / `X meaning` / `X explained`
fn _try_suffix_research(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 2 { return 0 }
    let last = tokens[len(tokens) - 1]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(last, "definition") == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(last, "meaning")    == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(last, "explained")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 0, len(tokens) - 1)
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "what is X" / "what are X" / "what was X" / "what were X" (existing)
fn _try_what_is(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    let t0 = tokens[0]
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "what") == 0 { return 0 }
    let t1 = tokens[1]
    let is_form = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "is")  == 1 { is_form = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "are") == 1 { is_form = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "was") == 1 { is_form = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "were") == 1 { is_form = 1 }
    if is_form == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// ---- relate matchers -----------------------------------------------------

// "how does X relate to Y"
fn _try_how_does_relate_to(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 6 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "how")  == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "does") == 0 { return 0 }
    let rel_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "relate", 3)
    if rel_idx < 0 { return 0 }
    let x = _gp_join(tokens, 2, rel_idx)
    if len(x) == 0 { return 0 }
    let y_start = rel_idx + 1
    if y_start < len(tokens) {
        if str_eq_bytes(tokens[y_start], "to") == 1 { y_start = y_start + 1 }
    }
    let y = _gp_join(tokens, y_start, len(tokens))
    if len(y) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_relate(x, y, raw, "grammar")
}

// "how are X and Y related"
fn _try_how_are_related(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 5 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "how") == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "are") == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[len(tokens) - 1], "related") == 0 { return 0 }
    let and_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "and", 3)
    if and_idx < 0 { return 0 }
    if and_idx >= len(tokens) - 2 { return 0 }
    let a = _gp_join(tokens, 2, and_idx)
    let b = _gp_join(tokens, and_idx + 1, len(tokens) - 1)
    if len(a) == 0 { return 0 }
    if len(b) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_relate(a, b, raw, "grammar")
}

// N-word noun-prefix + "between X and Y" -> RELATE
// - connection between / link between / association between /
//   similarities between / difference between / differences between
fn _try_relate_between(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 5 { return 0 }
    let t0 = tokens[0]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "connection")   == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "link")         == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "association")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "similarities") == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "difference")   == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "differences")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "between") == 0 { return 0 }
    let and_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "and", 3)
    if and_idx < 0 { return 0 }
    let a = _gp_join(tokens, 2, and_idx)
    let b = _gp_join(tokens, and_idx + 1, len(tokens))
    if len(a) == 0 { return 0 }
    if len(b) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_relate(a, b, raw, "grammar")
}

// "compare X and Y" / "comparison of X and Y"
fn _try_compare(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    let t0 = tokens[0]
    let start = 0 - 1
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "compare") == 1 { start = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "comparison") == 1 {
        if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "of") == 1 { start = 2 }
    }
    if start < 0 { return 0 }
    let and_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "and", start + 1)
    if and_idx < 0 { return 0 }
    let a = _gp_join(tokens, start, and_idx)
    let b = _gp_join(tokens, and_idx + 1, len(tokens))
    if len(a) == 0 { return 0 }
    if len(b) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_relate(a, b, raw, "grammar")
}

// Infix "X vs Y" / "X versus Y" -> RELATE
fn _try_vs(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    let vs_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "vs", 1)
    if vs_idx < 0 { vs_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "versus", 1) }
    if vs_idx <= 0 { return 0 }
    if vs_idx >= len(tokens) - 1 { return 0 }
    let a = _gp_join(tokens, 0, vs_idx)
    let b = _gp_join(tokens, vs_idx + 1, len(tokens))
    if len(a) == 0 { return 0 }
    if len(b) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_relate(a, b, raw, "grammar")
}

// ---- contradict matchers -------------------------------------------------

// "contradictions in X" / "inconsistencies in X" -> CONTRADICT_SCAN (b=a)
fn _try_contradictions_in(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    let t0 = tokens[0]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "contradictions")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "inconsistencies") == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "in") == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_contradict_scan(topic, topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "conflicts about X" / "disagreements about X" -> CONTRADICT_SCAN (b=a)
fn _try_conflicts_about(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    let t0 = tokens[0]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "conflicts")     == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "disagreements") == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "about") == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_contradict_scan(topic, topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// "where does X conflict" -> CONTRADICT_SCAN X X
fn _try_where_does_conflict(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "where") == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "does")  == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[len(tokens) - 1], "conflict") == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens) - 1)
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_contradict_scan(topic, topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// ---- 2-topic does-relate/contradict (existing) --------------------------

fn _try_does_relate_or_contradict(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "does") == 0 { return 0 }
    let rel_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "relate", 1)
    let contra_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "contradict", 1)
    let verb_idx = 0 - 1
    let kind = NLK_RESEARCH  // placeholder
    if rel_idx >= 0 { verb_idx = rel_idx  kind = NLK_RELATE }
    if contra_idx >= 0 {
        // If BOTH present, use the earlier one.
        if verb_idx < 0 { verb_idx = contra_idx  kind = NLK_CONTRADICT_SCAN }
        else { if contra_idx < verb_idx { verb_idx = contra_idx  kind = NLK_CONTRADICT_SCAN } }
    }
    if verb_idx <= 1 { return 0 }
    // X = tokens[1..verb_idx)
    let x = _gp_join(tokens, 1, verb_idx)
    if len(x) == 0 { return 0 }
    // "to" is optional after "relate" (grammar accepts "relate Y" too).
    let y_start = verb_idx + 1
    if y_start < len(tokens) {
        if str_eq_bytes(tokens[y_start], "to") == 1 { y_start = y_start + 1 }
    }
    let y = _gp_join(tokens, y_start, len(tokens))
    if len(y) == 0 { return 0 }
    if kind == NLK_RELATE           { return sq_relate(x, y, raw, "grammar") }
    if kind == NLK_CONTRADICT_SCAN  { return sq_contradict_scan(x, y, raw, "grammar") }
    return 0
}

// "does X count as [a] Y" -> IS_A
fn _try_does_count_as(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 5 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "does") == 0 { return 0 }
    let count_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "count", 2)
    if count_idx < 2 { return 0 }
    if count_idx + 1 >= len(tokens) { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[count_idx + 1], "as") == 0 { return 0 }
    let x = _gp_join(tokens, 1, count_idx)
    if len(x) == 0 { return 0 }
    let y_start = count_idx + 2
    if y_start < len(tokens) {
        // strip optional leading "a" / "an" from Y
        if str_eq_bytes(tokens[y_start], "a")  == 1 { y_start = y_start + 1 }
        else { if str_eq_bytes(tokens[y_start], "an") == 1 { y_start = y_start + 1 } }
    }
    let y = _gp_join(tokens, y_start, len(tokens))
    if len(y) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_is_a(x, y, raw, "grammar")
}

// ---- is_a matchers -------------------------------------------------------

// "is X considered [a/an] Y" -> IS_A
fn _try_is_considered(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "is") == 0 { return 0 }
    let c_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "considered", 2)
    if c_idx < 2 { return 0 }
    let x = _gp_join(tokens, 1, c_idx)
    if len(x) == 0 { return 0 }
    let y_start = c_idx + 1
    if y_start < len(tokens) {
        if str_eq_bytes(tokens[y_start], "a")  == 1 { y_start = y_start + 1 }
        else { if str_eq_bytes(tokens[y_start], "an") == 1 { y_start = y_start + 1 } }
    }
    let y = _gp_join(tokens, y_start, len(tokens))
    if len(y) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_is_a(x, y, raw, "grammar")
}

// "is X kind of Y" / "is X type of Y" (no "a" before kind/type) -> IS_A
fn _try_is_kind_type_of(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 5 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "is") == 0 { return 0 }
    // find kind/type followed by "of" at position >= 2
    let i = 2
    let hit = 0 - 1
    while i < len(tokens) - 2 {
        let ti = tokens[i]
        if str_eq_bytes(ti, "kind") == 1 {
            if str_eq_bytes(tokens[i + 1], "of") == 1 { hit = i  i = len(tokens) }
        }
        if hit < 0 {
            if str_eq_bytes(ti, "type") == 1 {
                if str_eq_bytes(tokens[i + 1], "of") == 1 { hit = i  i = len(tokens) }
            }
        }
        if hit < 0 { i = i + 1 }
    }
    if hit < 2 { return 0 }
    let x = _gp_join(tokens, 1, hit)
    let y = _gp_join(tokens, hit + 2, len(tokens))
    if len(x) == 0 { return 0 }
    if len(y) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_is_a(x, y, raw, "grammar")
}

// "is X a Y" / "is X an Y". Also strips leading "kind of" / "type of"
// from Y so "is earth a kind of planet" -> x=earth y=planet.
fn _try_is_a(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "is") == 0 { return 0 }
    // Find "a" or "an" at position >= 2 (so X is at least 1 token).
    let a_idx = 0 - 1
    let i = 2
    while i < len(tokens) - 1 {
        if str_eq_bytes(tokens[i], "a")  == 1 { a_idx = i i = len(tokens) }
        else { if str_eq_bytes(tokens[i], "an") == 1 { a_idx = i i = len(tokens) }
               else { i = i + 1 } }
    }
    if a_idx < 2 { return 0 }
    let x = _gp_join(tokens, 1, a_idx)
    let y_start = a_idx + 1
    // strip leading "kind of" / "type of"
    if y_start + 1 < len(tokens) {
        let s0 = tokens[y_start]
        let s1 = tokens[y_start + 1]
        if str_eq_bytes(s1, "of") == 1 {
            if str_eq_bytes(s0, "kind") == 1 { y_start = y_start + 2 }
            else { if str_eq_bytes(s0, "type") == 1 { y_start = y_start + 2 } }
        }
    }
    let y = _gp_join(tokens, y_start, len(tokens))
    if len(x) == 0 { return 0 }
    if len(y) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_is_a(x, y, raw, "grammar")
}

// Declarative: "X is a Y" / "X is an Y". Runs LATE so question-starting
// matchers get first crack. Requires X non-empty (`is` not at position 0).
fn _try_declarative_is_a(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    // find `is a` or `is an` where the `is` is at position >= 1
    let hit = _gp_find_pair(tokens, "is", "a",  1)
    if hit < 0 { hit = _gp_find_pair(tokens, "is", "an", 1) }
    if hit < 1 { return 0 }
    if hit + 2 >= len(tokens) { return 0 }
    let x = _gp_join(tokens, 0, hit)
    let y = _gp_join(tokens, hit + 2, len(tokens))
    if len(x) == 0 { return 0 }
    if len(y) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_is_a(x, y, raw, "grammar")
}

// ---- who / when / where --------------------------------------------------

// "who is X" / "who are X" -> RESEARCH filtered to person-kind atoms
fn _try_who_is(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "who") == 0 { return 0 }
    let t1 = tokens[1]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "is")   == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "are")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "was")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "were") == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research_filtered(topic, "person", raw, "grammar")
}

// "when did X" / "when was X" / "when is X" -> RESEARCH filtered "event"
fn _try_when(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "when") == 0 { return 0 }
    let t1 = tokens[1]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "did")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "was")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "is")   == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "were") == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "are")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research_filtered(topic, "event", raw, "grammar")
}

// "where is X" / "where are X" -> RESEARCH filtered "place"
fn _try_where_is(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "where") == 0 { return 0 }
    let t1 = tokens[1]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "is")   == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "are")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "was")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "were") == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research_filtered(topic, "place", raw, "grammar")
}

// "why X" (loose form)
fn _try_why(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 2 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "why") == 0 { return 0 }
    let topic = _gp_join(tokens, 1, len(tokens))
    if len(topic) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_research(topic, raw, "grammar")
}

// ---- retract matchers ----------------------------------------------------

// Single-word RETRACT verbs: retract / forget / remove / delete / unlearn
// / withdraw. Also "forget about X" strips "about". "retract fact X"
// strips "fact".
fn _try_retract_family(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 2 { return 0 }
    let t0 = tokens[0]
    let is_verb = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "retract")  == 1 { is_verb = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "forget")   == 1 { is_verb = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "remove")   == 1 { is_verb = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "delete")   == 1 { is_verb = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "unlearn")  == 1 { is_verb = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "withdraw") == 1 { is_verb = 1 }
    if is_verb == 0 { return 0 }
    let start = 1
    // "retract fact X" -> strip "fact"
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "retract") == 1 {
        if len(tokens) >= 3 {
            if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "fact") == 1 { start = 2 }
        }
    }
    // "forget about X" -> strip "about"
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "forget") == 1 {
        if len(tokens) >= 3 {
            if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "about") == 1 { start = 2 }
        }
    }
    let label = _gp_join(tokens, start, len(tokens))
    if len(label) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_retract(label, raw, "grammar")
}

// ---- install / add / load / enable / activate / import ------------------

// "install/add/load/import/enable capsule X" / "install pack X"
// "install/add/load/enable/activate skill X"
fn _try_install_family(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    let t0 = tokens[0]
    let cap_ok = 0
    let sk_ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "install") == 1 { cap_ok = 1  sk_ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "add")     == 1 { cap_ok = 1  sk_ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "load")    == 1 { cap_ok = 1  sk_ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "import")  == 1 { cap_ok = 1  sk_ok = 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "enable")  == 1 { cap_ok = 1  sk_ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "activate")== 1 { cap_ok = 0  sk_ok = 1 }
    if cap_ok == 0 { if sk_ok == 0 { return 0 } }
    let t1 = tokens[1]
    let name = _gp_join(tokens, 2, len(tokens))
    if len(name) == 0 { return 0 }
    if cap_ok == 1 {
        if str_eq_bytes(t1, "capsule") == 1 { return sq_capsule_install(name, raw, "grammar") }
        if str_eq_bytes(t1, "pack")    == 1 { return sq_capsule_install(name, raw, "grammar") }
    }
    if sk_ok == 1 {
        if str_eq_bytes(t1, "skill") == 1 { return sq_skill_install(name, raw, "grammar") }
    }
    return 0
}

// ---- list variants -------------------------------------------------------

// "list capsules" / "list capsule" / "list skills" / "list skill"
// / "list all capsules" / "list all skills"
fn _try_list(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 2 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "list") == 0 { return 0 }
    let idx = 1
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "all") == 1 {
        if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
        idx = 2
    }
    let t = tokens[idx]
    if str_eq_bytes(t, "capsules") == 1 { return sq_capsule_list(raw, "grammar") }
    if str_eq_bytes(t, "capsule")  == 1 { return sq_capsule_list(raw, "grammar") }
    if str_eq_bytes(t, "skills")   == 1 { return sq_skill_list(raw, "grammar") }
    if str_eq_bytes(t, "skill")    == 1 { return sq_skill_list(raw, "grammar") }
    return 0
}

// "show capsules" / "show all capsules" / "show skills" / "show all skills"
fn _try_show(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 2 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "show") == 0 { return 0 }
    let idx = 1
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "all") == 1 {
        if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
        idx = 2
    }
    let t = tokens[idx]
    if str_eq_bytes(t, "capsules") == 1 { return sq_capsule_list(raw, "grammar") }
    if str_eq_bytes(t, "capsule")  == 1 { return sq_capsule_list(raw, "grammar") }
    if str_eq_bytes(t, "skills")   == 1 { return sq_skill_list(raw, "grammar") }
    if str_eq_bytes(t, "skill")    == 1 { return sq_skill_list(raw, "grammar") }
    return 0
}

// "what capsules are installed" / "what skills are available"
fn _try_what_are(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "what") == 0 { return 0 }
    let t1 = tokens[1]
    let is_cap = 0
    let is_sk  = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "capsules") == 1 { is_cap = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "skills")   == 1 { is_sk  = 1 }
    if is_cap == 0 { if is_sk == 0 { return 0 } }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[2], "are") == 0 { return 0 }
    let t3 = tokens[3]
    let good = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t3, "installed") == 1 { good = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t3, "available") == 1 { good = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t3, "there")     == 1 { good = 1 }
    if good == 0 { return 0 }
    if is_cap == 1 { return sq_capsule_list(raw, "grammar") }
    return sq_skill_list(raw, "grammar")
}

// "which capsules do i have" / "which skills do i have"
fn _try_which_do_i_have(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 5 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "which") == 0 { return 0 }
    let t1 = tokens[1]
    let is_cap = 0
    let is_sk  = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "capsules") == 1 { is_cap = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "skills")   == 1 { is_sk  = 1 }
    if is_cap == 0 { if is_sk == 0 { return 0 } }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[2], "do")   == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[3], "i")    == 0 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[4], "have") == 0 { return 0 }
    if is_cap == 1 { return sq_capsule_list(raw, "grammar") }
    return sq_skill_list(raw, "grammar")
}

// Bare 2-token: "installed capsules" / "available capsules"
// / "installed skills" / "available skills"
fn _try_installed_available(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) != 2 { return 0 }
    let t0 = tokens[0]
    let adj = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "installed") == 1 { adj = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "available") == 1 { adj = 1 }
    if adj == 0 { return 0 }
    let t1 = tokens[1]
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "capsules") == 1 { return sq_capsule_list(raw, "grammar") }
    if str_eq_bytes(t1, "skills")   == 1 { return sq_skill_list(raw, "grammar") }
    return 0
}

// ---- skill run variants --------------------------------------------------

// "run [skill] X on Y" -- existing shape.
fn _try_run_skill(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 3 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "run") == 0 { return 0 }
    let skill_start = 1
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "skill") == 1 { skill_start = 2 }
    if skill_start >= len(tokens) { return 0 }
    let on_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "on", skill_start)
    if on_idx < 0 {
        // "run X with Y" -- accept "with" as an alias
        on_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "with", skill_start)
        if on_idx < 0 { return 0 }
    }
    if on_idx == skill_start { return 0 }
    let skill_name = _gp_join(tokens, skill_start, on_idx)
    let arg = _gp_join(tokens, on_idx + 1, len(tokens))
    if len(skill_name) == 0 { return 0 }
    if len(arg) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_skill_run(skill_name, arg, raw, "grammar")
}

// "execute [skill] X on Y" / "use [skill] X on Y" / "invoke [skill] X on Y"
fn _try_execute_use_invoke(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    let t0 = tokens[0]
    let ok = 0
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "execute") == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "use")     == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if str_eq_bytes(t0, "invoke")  == 1 { ok = 1 }
    if ok == 0 { return 0 }
    let skill_start = 1
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[1], "skill") == 1 {
        if len(tokens) < 5 { return 0 }
        skill_start = 2
    }
    let on_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "on", skill_start)
    if on_idx < 0 { return 0 }
    if on_idx == skill_start { return 0 }
    let skill_name = _gp_join(tokens, skill_start, on_idx)
    let arg = _gp_join(tokens, on_idx + 1, len(tokens))
    if len(skill_name) == 0 { return 0 }
    if len(arg) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_skill_run(skill_name, arg, raw, "grammar")
}

// "apply X to Y" -> SKILL_RUN
fn _try_apply_to(tokens, raw) {
    if len(tokens) < 4 { return 0 }
    if str_eq_bytes(tokens[0], "apply") == 0 { return 0 }
    let to_idx = _gp_find_token(tokens, "to", 2)
    if to_idx < 2 { return 0 }
    let skill_name = _gp_join(tokens, 1, to_idx)
    let arg = _gp_join(tokens, to_idx + 1, len(tokens))
    if len(skill_name) == 0 { return 0 }
    if len(arg) == 0 { return 0 }
    return sq_skill_run(skill_name, arg, raw, "grammar")
}

// ---- entry point ----------------------------------------------------------

// Match patterns in priority order. First hit wins. Fall through to
// UNPARSED so the caller can escalate to the LLM fallback.
fn grammar_parse(text) {
    if _gp_is_blank(text) == 1 { return sq_none(text, "grammar") }
    // Slash-commands bypass the NL layer entirely.
    if _gp_slash_prefixed(text) == 1 { return sq_unparsed(text) }
    let raw_tokens = _gp_tokenize(text)
    if len(raw_tokens) == 0 { return sq_none(text, "grammar") }
    // Filler-only (greeting / interjection) -> NONE
    if _gp_all_fillers(raw_tokens) == 1 { return sq_none(text, "grammar") }
    // Strip common polite/filler preambles so `please tell me about X`
    // parses like `tell me about X`. Never touches `not`.
    let tokens = _gp_strip_preamble(raw_tokens)
    if len(tokens) == 0 { return sq_none(text, "grammar") }
    // After stripping, another filler check catches greetings-plus-punc
    // like `please hi`.
    if _gp_all_fillers(tokens) == 1 { return sq_none(text, "grammar") }
    // ---- ordered pattern list (more-specific FIRST) ------------------
    // 5+ token prefixes
    let r = _try_what_do_you_know_about(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_what_is_the_meaning_of(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_what_can_you_say_about(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_what_is_the_relationship_between(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // 4-token prefixes
    r = _try_scan_for_contradictions_about(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_give_me_info(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // 3-token specific prefixes
    r = _try_tell_me_about(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_key_points_about(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_find_contradictions_in(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // multi-token "how ..." / "what does ..." shapes
    r = _try_how_does_relate_to(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_how_are_related(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_how_does_x_work(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_why_is_x_important(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_what_does_x_mean(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_where_does_conflict(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // relate-between / compare / contradict-scan noun-prefixes
    r = _try_relate_between(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_compare(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_contradictions_in(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_conflicts_about(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // Research 2-token noun prefixes (history of, origin of, ...)
    r = _try_research_prefix2(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_information_prefix(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_elaborate_expand_on(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_know_about(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // Single-word RESEARCH verbs (explain / describe / define)
    r = _try_explain_describe_define(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // does-count-as (IS_A) before does-relate-or-contradict
    r = _try_does_count_as(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_does_relate_or_contradict(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // is-considered before is-a; is-a before is-kind-type-of so
    // "is X a kind of Y" (with article) routes to is-a (which strips
    // "kind of" / "type of" from Y). is-kind-type-of handles only the
    // article-less form "is X kind of Y".
    r = _try_is_considered(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_is_a(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_is_kind_type_of(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // question-word starts
    r = _try_who_is(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_when(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_where_is(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // "what is X" catch-all (must come AFTER the more-specific "what ..."
    // matchers so "what is the meaning of X" doesn't get eaten as
    // topic="the meaning of X")
    r = _try_what_is(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // vs / versus (infix)
    r = _try_vs(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // Admin verbs
    r = _try_retract_family(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_install_family(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // list / show / what/which capsules-or-skills; bare 2-token forms
    r = _try_list(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_show(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_what_are(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_which_do_i_have(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_installed_available(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // skill run variants
    r = _try_run_skill(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_execute_use_invoke(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    r = _try_apply_to(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // Suffix RESEARCH form (X definition / X meaning / X explained)
    r = _try_suffix_research(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // Declarative "X is a Y" -- runs late so questions don't get shadowed
    r = _try_declarative_is_a(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    // WHY has the loosest pattern; try it last so it doesn't shadow
    // more specific matchers.
    r = _try_why(tokens, text)
    if r != 0 { return r }
    return sq_unparsed(text)
}
